# {{name}}

A hanafubuki-agent plugin written in Python, with
[pykardia](https://github.com/licyk/pykardia)'s guest SDK (MIT OR
Apache-2.0). It contributes a tool (`count_words`) and a prompt fragment.
`package/` is the plugin the Agent installs; `plugin.py` is its source.

Export the guest into the package: a zipapp that bundles the SDK, which the
Agent runs with `python3` from the `PATH`. The export needs a pykardia that
speaks kardia-guest/2 (its repository's `main`; PyPI's 0.1.0 is older):

```sh
python3 -m pip install git+https://github.com/licyk/pykardia
python3 -m pykardia.guest.export process plugin.py Plugin package/{{name}}.pyz
```

Check it, start it once, then run it in the Agent and reload it at each new
export until Ctrl+C:

```sh
hanafubuki-agent plugins validate package --run
hanafubuki-agent plugins dev package
```

See [Writing plugins](https://licyk.github.io/hanafubuki-agent/docs/writing-plugins/).
